# iolbox macOS/Lima guest profile table.
#
# This file is data, not provisioning logic.  iolbox-mac.sh reads one row for
# the selected profile and uses the named pin file, template, guest steps,
# kernel series, support status, and baseline canary expectation.  Adding a
# candidate guest is therefore one table row plus its pin/template assets;
# the Debian profiles deliberately reuse the generic Debian guest steps.
#
# Fields, in order:
#   name | guest | pin env | Lima template | multiarch step | kernel-hold step
#   | kernel series | status | canary verdict | canary basis
#   | image URL variable | image SHA256 variable | URL token | SHA token
#
# The canary expectation is for the measured macOS 13.5 baseline.  Debian 12
# is a CANDIDATE: its 6.1 kernel is inferred safe from the 6.3 threshold but
# has never been executed on Apple Silicon Rosetta.  Debian 13 is BLOCKED on
# that baseline because its 6.12 kernel is expected to emit AT_RSEQ_ALIGN.
IOLBOX_PROFILE_TABLE='jammy|Ubuntu 22.04|pinned-image.env|iolbox-jammy.yaml|10-multiarch.sh|20-kernel-hold.sh|5.15|PROVEN on hardware (M0)|PASS|measured on M0|IOLBOX_JAMMY_IMAGE_URL|IOLBOX_JAMMY_IMAGE_SHA256|@IOLBOX_JAMMY_IMAGE_URL@|@IOLBOX_JAMMY_IMAGE_SHA256@
debian12|Debian 12 bookworm|pinned-image-debian12.env|iolbox-bookworm.yaml|10-multiarch-debian.sh|20-kernel-hold-debian.sh|6.1|CANDIDATE, UNVERIFIED|PASS|inferred from the 6.3 threshold; never executed on Apple Silicon Rosetta|IOLBOX_DEBIAN12_IMAGE_URL|IOLBOX_DEBIAN12_IMAGE_SHA256|@IOLBOX_DEBIAN12_IMAGE_URL@|@IOLBOX_DEBIAN12_IMAGE_SHA256@
debian13|Debian 13 trixie|pinned-image-debian13.env|iolbox-trixie.yaml|10-multiarch-debian.sh|20-kernel-hold-debian.sh|6.12.94|BLOCKED on macOS 13.5|FAIL_AUXV|inferred; Linux >= 6.3 emits AT_RSEQ_ALIGN and macOS 13.5 Rosetta aborts|IOLBOX_DEBIAN13_IMAGE_URL|IOLBOX_DEBIAN13_IMAGE_SHA256|@IOLBOX_DEBIAN13_IMAGE_URL@|@IOLBOX_DEBIAN13_IMAGE_SHA256@'
